a and the United Kingdom. Easter bread is also a common tradition amongst the Assyrian diaspora."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-paska-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paska_(bread)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Belarusian cuisine","links":[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cold beet soup","dish/cold-beet-soup"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kalduny","dish/kalduny"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Krupnik (soup)","dish/krupnik-soup"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Šakotis","dish/sakotis"],["Salceson","dish/salceson"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"],["Zatiruha","dish/zatiruha"],["Zrazy","dish/zrazy"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a1/Martiniouk_Paska.JPG/500px-Martiniouk_Paska.JPG","w":500,"h":332,"by":"AMartiniouk","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martiniouk_Paska.JPG"}},"dish/pyeonsu":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pyeonsu","n":"Pyeonsu","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from North Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Pyeonsu is a square-shaped mandu (dumpling) in Korean cuisine. It is a food typically served in summer, served chilled, and dipped in soy sauce and vinegar. The city of Gaeseong is famous for its pyeonsu."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pyeonsu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyeonsu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["North Korean cuisine","cuisine/north-korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from North Korean cuisine","links":[["Injo-gogi-bap","dish/injo-gogi-bap"],["Paensae","dish/paensae"],["Pyongyang Raengmyon","dish/pyongyang-raengmyon"],["Sungeo-guk","dish/sungeo-guk"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/be/Pyeonsu.jpg/500px-Pyeonsu.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"행복가족","lic":"CC BY 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyeonsu.jpg"}},"dish/stuffed-squash":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/stuffed-squash","n":"Stuffed squash","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 8 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Stuffed squash, courgette, marrow, zucchini or mahshi kusa is a dish common in Egypt, the Levant and the Balkans. It is a kind of dolma consisting of various kinds of squash or zucchini, stuffed with rice and sometimes meat, and cooked on the stovetop or in the oven. The meat version is served hot, as a main course. The meatless version is considered an \"olive-oil dish\" and is often eaten at room temperature or warm."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-stuffed-squash"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuffed_squash"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cypriot cuisine","cuisine/cypriot-cuisine"],["Egyptian cuisine","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine"],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"],["Jordanian cuisine","cuisine/jordanian-cuisine"],["Lebanese cuisine","cuisine/lebanese-cuisine"],["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine"],["Palestinian cuisine","cuisine/palestinian-cuisine"],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Zucchini","ingredient/zucchini"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kopiaste","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kopiaste.org","note":"Long-running blog of Greek and Cypriot home recipes.","url":"https://www.kopiaste.org/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chez Nermine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cheznermine.com","note":"Egyptian recipes and the stories behind them from Egyptian American cook Nermine.","url":"https://cheznermine.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Amira's Pantry","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"amiraspantry.com","note":"Egyptian section of Amira's recipe blog, with koshari, hawawshi, feteer and sweets.","url":"https://amiraspantry.com/tag/egyptian-cuisine/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Cypriot cuisine","links":[["Fasolada","dish/fasolada"],["Mujaddara","dish/mujaddara"]]}]}}